Hello again!

With a rather quick and dirty adaptation of my stepwise function
(getting rid of the update function and calling occu each time with a
newly created formula string) I was able to resolve the error from
before.

Unfortunately I ran into another problem:

I am storing all the models that are ran by the stepwise function in a
list to later run fitList and modSel.

The fitList call runs fine with each of my outputs, like:

fitlst <- fitList (fits = GCKIr$modlst)

The modSel function gives me some problems though:

modsel <- modSel(fitlst)

If I call it for species with a set of 25 or 28 models everything is
fine and I get the appropriate results. If I call it for a species
with only 5 models I get the following error message:

Error in `$<-.data.frame`(`*tmp*`, "formula", value = c("~Lndar_1kmZ +
FOR1_DA_1KZ + CR_CL_3Z + DATE_JUL + OCODES ~ UTM_E + ",  :
  replacement has 2 rows, data has 5

Do you have any idea what might be causing this/ how I could adopt my
code to avoid this?

Thanks again,
Richard

